  "meta": {
    "title": "Point Nemo: The Loneliest Place on Earth 🌊🚀😱",
    "description": "Point Nemo 🌊 is the spot in the ocean farthest from any land: about 2,688 km from the nearest islands (Ducie Island, Motu Nui near Easter Island, and Maher Island off Antarctica) 😱 No regular ship or air routes pass within 400 km, so sometimes the closest humans are astronauts on the International Space Station flying overhead 🚀 It's also a 'spacecraft cemetery', where old satellites and space stations are sent to crash safely 🛰️",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "The nearest humans are in SPACE 🚀😱",
      "Would you sail to Point Nemo? 👇",
      "Which remote place next? 🗺️"
    ],
